WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.476
"Risks and Benefits of
Nicotinamide (NAM), a NAD+ Booster"

00:00:06.967 --> 00:00:11.920
Ever since nicotinamide (NAM)
was also shown to cure pellagra,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:19.800
both nicotinic acid, NA, and NAM have been
collectively referred to as niacin or vitamin B3,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.600
though they are
distinct compounds.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.320
For example, NAM is not plagued by
the same kind of hot flash reaction.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.560
(Facial flushing attributed to
niacinamide in some older studies

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:35.360
was likely due to a less purified
form contaminated with residual NA.)

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.760
The relative capacity of NA versus
NAM to generate NAD+ is unclear.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.720
Neither has been shown
to boost sirtuin activity,

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.840
but both do extend the
lifespan of C. elegans.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.080
I couldn’t find any longevity
trials for NA in rodents;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.600
however, NAM was put to the test
and failed to prolong the lives of mice.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.000
What clinical effects might
we expect in people?

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.520
Previously, I explored the proven anti-
aging effects for topical nicotinamide

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:09.920
on the skin and the remarkable ability of
oral nicotinamide to help prevent skin cancer.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.360
I also noted it failed to
prevent type 1 diabetes,

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.440
despite promising mouse data,

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.760
though it may help preserve
residual function in people

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.760
newly diagnosed with
type 1 diabetes,

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.040
but apparently not enough
to affect blood sugar control.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.200
What about its use
as a NAD+ booster?

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.800
In those with
mitochondrial myopathy,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.400
NA raised muscle NAD+ levels and
improved mitochondrial and muscle function,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:39.640
but in healthy individuals,
muscle NAD+ levels didn’t budge.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.520
However, the average age of individuals
in the control group was 50.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.760
What about in older adults whose muscle
NAD+ levels might potentially be lower?

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:53.880
Four NAD+ precursors were tested
in older adults averaging in their 70s:

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.680
tryptophan, NA, NAM, and NR.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:03.000
All four failed to improve
muscle strength or function,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.440
failed to affect mitochondrial function,

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:09.760
and failed to even nudge
NAD+ levels in their muscles.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.520
Why not give it a try anyway?
Again, side effects.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.960
Like NA, high-dose NAM can cause
gastrointestinal disturbances

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.800
and signs of liver toxicity….

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.920
However, NAM may result in more
issues involving methylation.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.360
The first step in breaking down excess
NAM is to transfer a methyl group to it,

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.720
forming methylnicotinamide.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.880
Unfortunately,
methylnicotinamide is neurotoxic

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.040
and can cross the
blood-brain barrier.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.320
This may explain why NAM can exacerbate
Parkinson’s-like symptoms in rats

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.840
and why Parkinson’s patients
have higher levels

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.100
of the NAM-methylating
enzyme in their brains.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.160
And the same with Alzheimer's
brains for that matter.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:54.000
Excess NAM may also deplete
the body’s pool of methyl groups.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.480
If you read the Epigenetics chapter
in my book How Not to Age,

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:02.920
you may remember that DNA methylation is
critical for the regulation of gene expression.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.360
Epigenetic changes caused by
NAM-induced methyl depletion

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.160
have been blamed as the reason
why rats fed megadoses of NAM

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.840
suffer from fatty livers
and swollen kidneys,

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.560
but that was at a human-equivalent dose
far exceeding what people might take.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.520
Is there any evidence that
more modest NAM supplementation

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.560
might affect methylation in humans?

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:28.800
Yes, and even with a single
dose as low as 100 mg.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.400
Methylation also plays a key role in
breaking down fight-or-flight hormones

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.640
like noradrenaline and neurotransmitters
like serotonin and histamine.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:41.480
Within hours of a single
100 mg dose of NAM,

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:45.160
blood levels of all three
become elevated,

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:49.040
suggesting their metabolism was impaired
by the shunting of methyl groups

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.480
to deal with the excess NAM.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.200
Also noted was a significant
rise in homocysteine,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.880
which is a byproduct of
methylation reactions

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.720
and a risk factor for cardiovascular
disease and dementia.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:07.000
Another potential problem with NAM
is that it’s a sirtuin inhibitor.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:12.560
Wait, I thought the whole purpose of taking
NAD+ precursors is to boost sirtuin activity.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:17.920
Sirtuin enzymes use up
NAD+ and spit out NAM.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:24.000
This allows the body to recycle the NAM
back into NAD+ for further sirtuin use.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:29.040
But it also means the body can use
NAM as part of a negative feedback loop.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.920
Like a thermostat in the winter
that shuts down the furnace

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.440
when there’s too much heat,

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:39.320
the body shuts down NAD+ use by
sirtuins when it detects too much NAM.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.320
NAM pills didn’t exist
when our bodies evolved;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.560
so, in the wake of a
sudden wave of NAM,

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.680
the body must think its sirtuins are
churning out too much and dials them back.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:54.560
Perhaps, this explains why NAM
fails to prolong the lifespans of mice.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.560
When the sirtuin-suppressing effects of
NAM were first reported 20 years ago,

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.680
the researchers cautioned that
this could potentially lead to

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:07.642
“deleterious consequences of long-term
nicotinamide therapy in humans.”

